{"id": "EUVD-2026-59522", "enisaUuid": "b6965717-04df-3cd6-9570-4f89b3777089", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid1,raid10: fix deadlock in read error recovery path\n\nraid1d and raid10d may resubmit a split md cloned bio while handling\na read error. In this case, resubmitting the bio can lead to a deadlock\nif the array is suspended before md_handle_request() acquires an\nactive_io reference via percpu_ref_tryget_live().\n\nSince the cloned bio already holds an active_io reference,\ntrying to acquire another reference via percpu_ref_tryget_live()\ncan lead to a deadlock while the array is suspended.\n\nFix this by using percpu_ref_get() for md cloned bios.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/923a6f3172a362d6b2ff12386e376e0e47188f78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0889242775340e2c5b69b1590bd71335dd4fdeda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea2d1d2ebf60b70b602a92261a567d5fc4575eab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38777f014c37972868f1733a651c85288bb8a757", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b15c24f805339a585cfe7d72f446b7e88b9bcc0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xhm4-9f9x-w7xp", "CVE-2026-74375"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f68f17d-0430-3c23-b123-d9f4774ccedf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <ea2d1d2ebf60b70b602a92261a567d5fc4575eab"}, {"id": "2c9d22c1-4646-355e-ae68-6457f73428f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3478ad72-c05b-3ce2-9128-b2c6579f7f8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <923a6f3172a362d6b2ff12386e376e0e47188f78"}, {"id": "3dd886d2-322d-310f-951a-f2602c666273", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <38777f014c37972868f1733a651c85288bb8a757"}, {"id": "5699cf0f-474d-3a01-928f-e45c1c1f1f3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5704a7e1-a206-3473-b810-063a54924b15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <7b15c24f805339a585cfe7d72f446b7e88b9bcc0"}, {"id": "749a8f4f-f29e-39af-83d6-fe89133f3467", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "834cda99-9186-34a7-884f-6e45f0b9c069", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "870dd054-6c38-3cf6-80a3-163e0461d1b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "8929cbdf-57ad-3a1a-95b6-6b7be84f9a18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <0889242775340e2c5b69b1590bd71335dd4fdeda"}, {"id": "dce2a820-ac35-3fac-b9ff-511e8f9aa183", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "e1a7b866-ecea-3485-bf6e-80a6eb9fb011", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b6bb67cd-e5e6-30d9-a1f3-f6fc3fa6edfc", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}